Unscripted (the "Software") is source-available. The source is
published so it can be read, audited, modified and evaluated. It is not open
source: commercial use above the threshold in section 2 requires a paid licence.

"THE SOFTWARE" INCLUDES WHAT YOU MAKE OF IT. Any modified version, adaptation,
translation, port to another programming language, or work derived from the
Software in whole or in part is a "Derivative Work", and every permission and
every obligation in this licence applies to a Derivative Work exactly as it
applies to the Software.

You may fork it. Forking is expressly permitted by section 1 and needs no
permission. What forking does not do is end the obligation to licence: changing
the Software, renaming it, or rewriting it in another language does not produce
a work that falls outside these terms.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. FREE LICENCE (no payment, no registration)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Vigilant e.K. grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to use,
copy, modify and distribute the Software, and to distribute works built with it,
for any of the following:

  a) PRIVATE AND EDUCATIONAL USE
     Personal projects, study, teaching and academic research.

  b) GAME MODIFICATIONS
     Mods, total conversions and community tools for third-party games,
     including mods distributed for payment, provided the mod itself is the
     product and the Software is not sublicensed separately.

  c) NON-COMMERCIAL AND SMALL COMMERCIAL PROJECTS
     Any Product of a Small Organisation whose Qualifying Income has not yet
     reached EUR 200,000 (the "Threshold"). Below the Threshold no payment is
     due and no notification is required.

     A SMALL ORGANISATION is an individual, or an organisation whose total
     revenue and funding in its last completed financial year -- counted
     together with that of any parent company or group it belongs to -- was
     less than EUR 1,000,000.

     This free tier is for small teams. An organisation above that line needs a
     commercial licence for commercial use of the Software however little any
     single Product of theirs earns, because forty Products at EUR 150,000 is
     not a small team and per-Product accounting alone would not have said so.
     Subsections (a), (b), (d) and (e) apply to any organisation regardless of
     size: private and educational use, mods, evaluation and research
     publication are never gated on how large you are.

     QUALIFYING INCOME means the cumulative total, from the Product's first
     public availability onward and for its entire lifetime, of:
       - gross revenue you receive from the Product, before platform fees,
         refunds and tax; and
       - money received specifically to develop or publish that Product,
         including publisher advances, grants and platform funding.
     It does not include your other products, your other activities, or general
     investment in your company that is not tied to this Product.

     A PRODUCT is one game or application, together with everything sold as part
     of or as an addition to it: downloadable content, expansions, season passes,
     ports of it to other platforms, and re-releases of substantially the same
     work under any name. A sequel, or a different game that reuses the
     technology, is a separate Product with its own Threshold.

  d) EVALUATION
     Internal evaluation, prototyping and technical due diligence by any
     organisation, for up to 180 days, regardless of that organisation's size.

  e) RESEARCH PUBLICATION
     Reproducing results, publishing benchmarks and citing the Software.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. WHEN A COMMERCIAL LICENCE IS REQUIRED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A separate written commercial licence from Vigilant e.K. is required to ship,
operate or distribute a product that incorporates the Software or a Derivative
Work, in whole or in part, once that product exceeds the Threshold in
section 1(c).

A product built on a fork, on a port of the Software to another language, or on
a version with the names changed incorporates the Software for the purposes of
this section. The Threshold and the cases below apply to it unchanged.

The Threshold is measured per Product, not per company, and it is a lifetime
total rather than an annual one: a Product that earns EUR 60,000 a year reaches
it in the fourth year, and one that never reaches it never needs a commercial
licence, however long it sells.

Exceeding it does not invalidate work already done under the free licence; it
makes a commercial licence necessary for continued distribution or operation of
that Product. You have 90 days from the day the Threshold is reached to obtain
one, during which distribution may continue.

A commercial licence is also required, at any revenue, to:

  a) offer the Software or a Derivative Work as a hosted or managed service
     whose primary value is the Software's functionality;
  b) redistribute the Software or a Derivative Work as a middleware product,
     SDK, engine plugin or library under your own name or anyone else's;
  c) sublicense the Software or a Derivative Work to third parties other than as
     part of your own product;
  d) use the Software commercially at all, if you are not a Small Organisation
     as defined in section 1(c). Evaluation under section 1(d) remains free to
     any organisation for its 180 days.

Commercial terms, including per-title and site licences, support and source
escrow, are available from: info@vigilant-crs.de

Current list prices are published in the project's README rather than fixed
here, so that a change to them is not a change to this licence. They are
indicative: this section requires a written agreement, and that agreement
governs.

